      "side": 1,
      "message": "@ptosi@google.com What are the right semantics here in terms of some partitions being present and some not? Should the hash be omitted or something else?\n\nI\u0027m trying to think ahead, in case more partitions are added, eg. `initrd_vendor`, and making sure that selecting different 2 out of 3 cannot generate the same hash.\n\nThoughts?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "352e1cfe7ff73ab1b5c172a6345844b3725eb53f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6f840c12_ee78678f",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/dice.rs",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T14:40:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wouldn\u0027t `initrd_vendor` be loaded from disk by the kernel? If not and it\u0027s preloaded by the VMM, could it be packaged and signed at build time and become part of what we now consider `initrd`?\n\nIn general, I wouldn\u0027t include information about what is missing in the DICE inputs. So, for the code input, just hash _everything_ that is relevant to the next stage (and nothing more). Once we start using BCC descriptors, we should start recording which \"partitions\" were actually seen by pvmfw, to make it easy to parse.",
      "parentUuid": "a842dbf1_0407ab55",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "352e1cfe7ff73ab1b5c172a6345844b3725eb53f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad3f7174_1b1739e1",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/dice.rs",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T14:47:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "re initrd: Unclear, but if they needed to be signed by different entities and updated independently, separate partitions would be necessary.\n\nBasically what I\u0027m trying to avoid is blindly concatenating and running into:\n```\nhash(kernel, Some(initrd_normal), None) \u003d\u003d hash(kernel, None, Some(initrd_vendor))\n```\n\nAt that point we either need to include the `None` in the hash, or somehow tag the individual inputs, eg. \n```\nhash(kernel, concat(\"initrd|\", initrd_normal)) !\u003d hash(kernel, concat(\"initrd_vendor|\", initrd_vendor))\n```",
      "parentUuid": "6f840c12_ee78678f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "352e1cfe7ff73ab1b5c172a6345844b3725eb53f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cf4b527c_13b2d09f",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/dice.rs",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T15:21:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What about setting initrd part to zero when it\u0027s None? Then\n\n- kernel, Some(initrd_normal), None \u003d | kernel | initrd | 00\n- kernel, None, Some(initrd_vendor) \u003d | kernel | 00 | initrd",
      "parentUuid": "ad3f7174_1b1739e1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "352e1cfe7ff73ab1b5c172a6345844b3725eb53f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a21d3a75_6e4a4efc",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/dice.rs",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059815
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T17:08:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That would make sense to me. IIUC, Pierre is suggesting encoding this information in the `code_descriptor` string. If that\u0027s the DICE way, then we should probably do that.\n\n * kernel, Some(initrd_normal), None\n   * code_hash \u003d hash(kernel | initrd_normal)\n   * code_descriptor \u003d \"kernel,initrd\"\n * kernel, None, Some(initrd_vendor)\n   * code_hash \u003d hash(kernel | initrd_vendor)\n   * code_descriptor \u003d \"kernel,initrd_vendor\"\n \nIs that right, Pierre?",
      "parentUuid": "cf4b527c_13b2d09f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "352e1cfe7ff73ab1b5c172a6345844b3725eb53f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "654a9d2d_3baba283",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/dice.rs",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 33,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-31T17:41:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAICT, these would result in different BCCs (so attestation, if it didn\u0027t ignore the descriptors, could tell the different between the configurations) but identical CDIs if `hash(kernel | initrd_normal) \u003d\u003d hash(kernel | initrd_vendor)`.\n\n\u003e re initrd: Unclear, but if they needed to be signed by different entities and updated independently, separate partitions would be necessary.\n\nThat particular case should affect the CDIs by having different authority inputs, though.",
      "parentUuid": "ad3f7174_1b1739e1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 33,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 33,
        "endChar": 84
      },
